king the algebra on the decision threshold: cooperating beats defecting when 7q > 5, so q > 5/7. I'm also judging how strongly the two choices are correlated, which looks high given the identical setup, and I'm settling on passing.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through the twin prisoner's dilemma under evidential decision theory, using the payoffs CC = 2 years, DC = 0, CD = 5, DD = 4 with utility as negative years. I'm setting up the expected disutility of cooperating and defecting, with the correlation between the two choices tied to the probability q.\n\nI'm checking the algebra on the decision threshold: cooperating beats defecting when 7q > 5, so q > 5/7. I'm also judging how strongly the two choices are correlated, which looks high given the identical setup, and I'm settling on passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9419,"completion_tokens":776,"total_tokens":10195,"cost":0.053196,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.053196,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.037676,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01552},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":286,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}